# Alternatives for Optimization of Teaching-Learning Processes in Southeast Asian Universities.

**Authors:** Muhammadi, Ed.

## Abstract
Opening addresses, conference papers, and summaries of group discussions are contained in these proceedings. Papers include: challenges for higher education in southeast Asia (Makaminan Makagiansar); higher education in Asian countries today (Gwee Yee Hean); changing profiles of university students in southeast Asia (Nuanper Wichiarajote); a critical assessment of university teaching (Hulman Sinaga); curriculum development in southeast Asian universities, new approaches (Partomo M. Alibazah); and alternatives for teaching-learning processes (Ernesto O. Javier). Discussions addressed: national developmemt and optimization of teaching-learning processes; higher education institutions and optimization of teaching-learning processes; university students, teachers, and optimization;  and curriculum development and optimization. (MSE)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=ED149695

